    {
      "id": 0,
      "sentence": "At the start of Milan Fashion Week, Gucci unveiled a lookbook instead of a traditional runway show.",
      "paragraph_id": 0,
      "word_count": 17,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 7.125,
      "duration": 7.125,
      "phoneme_count": 100
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "sentence": "Photographed by Catherine Opie, it featured 37 distinct characters dressed in looks inspired by the Gucci archive.",
      "paragraph_id": 0,
      "word_count": 17,
      "start_time": 7.125,
      "end_time": 15.95,
      "duration": 8.825,
      "phoneme_count": 121
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "sentence": "Among La Famiglia, as the group was called, was \u201cMilanesa,\u201d who wore a knee-length fur coat with a gold chain belt and carried a crocodile-print bag, and \u201cSciura\u201d (pronounced shoo-rah), which is local dialect for a Milanese woman now generally considered to have bold and bourgeois taste.",
      "paragraph_id": 0,
      "word_count": 47,
      "start_time": 15.95,
      "end_time": 35.125,
      "duration": 19.175,
      "phoneme_count": 287
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "sentence": "Archetypes of Milanese women have inspired countless runway collections and imitators, and they have been used to market fashion brands in the past.",
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "word_count": 23,
      "start_time": 35.125,
      "end_time": 45.375,
      "duration": 10.25,
      "phoneme_count": 149
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "sentence": "But who are they, really?",
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "word_count": 5,
      "start_time": 45.375,
      "end_time": 47.55,
      "duration": 2.175,
      "phoneme_count": 23
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "sentence": "Do \u201cSciura\u201d still exist?",
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "word_count": 4,
      "start_time": 47.55,
      "end_time": 49.975,
      "duration": 2.425,
      "phoneme_count": 28
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "sentence": "What does it mean to dress like a \u201cMilanesa\u201d today?",
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "word_count": 10,
      "start_time": 49.975,
      "end_time": 53.4,
      "duration": 3.425,
      "phoneme_count": 51
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "sentence": "\u201cIn the 1980s, you used to be able to recognize a Milanese woman for her uniform,\u201d said Carla Sozzani, the founder of the Milanese concept store 10 Corso Como.",
      "paragraph_id": 2,
      "word_count": 29,
      "start_time": 53.4,
      "end_time": 65.675,
      "duration": 12.275,
      "phoneme_count": 180
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "sentence": "The look was \u201cclassic,\u201d perhaps including a camel-colored cashmere coat, a twin set and pearls.",
      "paragraph_id": 2,
      "word_count": 15,
      "start_time": 65.675,
      "end_time": 72.625,
      "duration": 6.95,
      "phoneme_count": 96
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "sentence": "When J.J.",
      "paragraph_id": 3,
      "word_count": 2,
      "start_time": 72.625,
      "end_time": 74.425,
      "duration": 1.8,
      "phoneme_count": 11
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "sentence": "Martin, the founder of the La Double J label, moved to Milan from New York 24 years ago, the uniform for women consisted of, she said, \u201ca really crisp, men\u2019s button-down shirt tucked into a Prada full skirt, incredible sunglasses that were handmade, a beautiful handbag from Valextra, or something like that \u2014 no logo \u2014 with kitten heels.\u201d",
      "paragraph_id": 3,
      "word_count": 59,
      "start_time": 74.425,
      "end_time": 97.95,
      "duration": 23.525,
      "phoneme_count": 362
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "sentence": "\u201cOn a bicycle.",
